	(text_box "VBPW34S PIN photodiode, reverse biased 4.5 V, into a transimpedance amplifier: 10 kΩ -> 10 mV per µA, 2.2 pF -> 6.8 MHz with 3.5 dB of peaking at 4 MHz (sim/tia.cir;\n3.3 pF flattens it). Plug an external photodiode into J6 (cathode to the top pin). Light makes the output go positive. Aim it at the LED on another board's DAC 2 for\nthe lock-in-across-the-room experiment."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 299.72 0)
		(size 125.73 7.62)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29b8925a-d15d-589c-28e8-8520197924eb")
	)
	(text_box "Grounds: AGND and DRGND are one plane on this board. The converter sits on the analog side of the floorplan with the FPGA's bus the only digital\nthing near it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400.05 317.5 0)
		(size 110.49 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "63d74c61-4056-e7d9-4d4f-c8129ea76abc")
	)
	(text_box "A resistor at room temperature makes √(4kTR) of noise: 1.3 nV/√Hz at 100 Ω, 12.9 nV/√Hz at 10 kΩ. Switch one in (DIP) or plug your own into J5.\nWith both channels on the same resistor, the cross-spectrum averages away each amplifier's own noise and leaves the resistor's. Switch 0 Ω in to\nmeasure the amplifiers alone."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 299.72 0)
		(size 109.22 7.62)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6540dacb-e900-22b6-655f-05198066f81f")
	)
	(text_box "Each channel: SMA (50 Ω or high-Z, jumper) -> 100 Ω + diode clamp to the ±4.5 V rails -> source jumper (SMA / noise resistor / photodiode) -> two OPA1612 stages, each x1 or x10 by jumper (so x1, x10, x100; 1.1 nV/√Hz) -> U.FL monitor tap -> THS4521 fully-differential driver at gain 1 (a BAV99 across its inputs keeps an overload under its 1 V differential limit) -> 33 Ω + 22 pF -> AD9238 (2 Vpp\ndifferential about 1.65 V = AVDD/2; -3 dB at 23 MHz at x1, sim/adc_frontend.cir). The ADC's internal 1.0 V reference sets the 2 Vpp span (SENSE = GND); SHARED_REF ties both channels to one reference so their gains match for the cross-correlation experiment. Both sample clocks come from the FPGA so the gateware owns the phase."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 340.36 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f4c913e7-64b5-6611-5bee-6e5118af638e")
	)
